FINAL ANSWER:
## Reviewer recommendation for `lib/index.js`

**Primary reviewer: Troy Goode.** Troy has about 29 of the file's roughly 55 commits, counting the 28 under `<email redacted>` and 1 under an alias email. After I excluded the reformat commit, `git blame` still attributes 109 of 232 lines to Troy, about 47%. Troy also made the latest substantive change, "lib: annotate handlers" on 2026-04-10.

**Secondary reviewer: Douglas Christopher Wilson.** Doug has 4 commits and owns 36 lines in blame once the reformat is ignored, so they know the core logic. Their last commit to this file was 2017-10-04, so they may no longer be involved. Check that they are still around before you request their review.

### Risk notes
- **This file is the whole library.** `lib/` contains only `index.js`, and `package.json` sets it as `"main"`. All five test files (`test/test.js`, `test/vary.js`, `test/issue-2.js`, `test/error-response.js`, `test/example-app.js`) import it directly. Any change to it affects every consumer.
- **Bus factor for this file is effectively 1–2.** The history has about 25 authors, but most contributed one commit before 2018. Only Troy has touched the file in the last 6 months, and Troy's last commit was about 6.5 months ago, on 2026-04-10. Nobody has committed to it in the last 6 months. I can't tell from git history whether Troy is still actively maintaining it.
- **Ignore "Fiona Formatter" as an owner.** That author appears only on the 2026-04-12 style commit (`62628c0`), which rewrote 214 lines. The commit tells you nothing about who understands the code. I used `git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0` to get past it.

### Suggestions
1. Request Troy Goode as the required reviewer. If Troy is unavailable, find a current maintainer who can sign off, because the history shows no other recent contributor.
2. Ask the reviewer to run the full `test/` suite, since all of it exercises this one file.
3. After a review, consider having a second maintainer read the file. That would stop knowledge of the file from sitting with one person.

I analyzed only this file. I didn't run the project-level bus factor across the whole repo or launch the contributor-analyzer agent, because your question was about one file. I can run the full analysis if you want it.

