FINAL ANSWER:
**Troy Goode should review it, with Douglas Christopher Wilson as a second reader.** The rest of this answer is ranked by surviving lines in `lib/index.js`, as of 2026-04-12 (the latest commit date). `lib/` holds only this one file, so the figures for `lib/` are the same.

The file has 214 non-blank lines (238 counting blank lines).

| Person | Lines (non-blank) | Lines (counting blank) | Last commit at this path |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode, both addresses counted as one | 144 (67.3%) | 159 (66.8%) | 2026-04-10, active |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 (9.3%) | 22 (9.2%) | 2017-10-04, inactive |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 14 (6.5%) | 16 (6.7%) | 2015-05-28, inactive |

- **Troy Goode:** Troy is the top owner and the only active author. The 144 lines are a guess that two addresses are one person, based on names and addresses, and nothing is written to `.mailmap`. Unmerged, `<email redacted>` holds 132 lines (61.7%) and 147 counting blank lines (61.8%), with no commit at this path since 2016-08-23. `troy@laptop.example` holds 12 lines (5.6%) and 12 counting blank lines (5.0%), with the 2026-04-10 commit.
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson:** Douglas is the next-largest owner and has no commit at this path since 2017-10-04. Their last commit anywhere was 2021-09-07, so they have left this file but not the project.
- **Alejandro Caravaca Puchades:** Alejandro's 14 lines include 11 from `e64e854`, which Troy committed. The lines are credited to Alejandro. They appear under two names on one address (`alex94puchades`).

**What the numbers leave out**
- **Reformat commit:** `62628c0` rewrote 1,016 lines in 4 files, formatting only. It is left out of these figures.
  - Without that correction, `<email redacted>` drops to 111 lines (51.9%).
  - With both addresses merged, Troy drops to 123 lines (57.5%).
  - Troy is still the top owner either way.
- **ESLint commit:** `fcd2b56` ("switch to ESLint; clean up", Troy, 5 surviving lines) looks mechanical. It was not set aside.
- **Bus factor:** The bus factor for this file is 1, because Troy alone holds more than half of the lines. That is on the merged figure and the unmerged one, and it is still 1 without the reformat correction.
- **Orphaned code:** None. Troy is active and owns the file.

These counts show who wrote the lines that are still here, not who understands them. Review quality isn't something line counts can show.

I couldn't run `--for-diff` because you haven't made the change yet. Once you have a branch or commit, `--for-diff <base>..<head>` will list the people who wrote the specific lines your change replaces or deletes. That is more precise than file-wide ownership.

